{
  "subtype": "focus_inference",
  "implied_focus": "IT asset/equipment procurement spend captured in these expense records (what was bought, from whom, for whom, and for what use)",
  "per_column": [
    {
      "name": "asset_type_category",
      "supports_focus": true,
      "rationale": "Classifies the kind of asset purchased (laptop, server, cloud_service), a core facet of the procurement focus."
    },
    {
      "name": "vendor_or_manufacturer",
      "supports_focus": true,
      "rationale": "Identifies who supplied the asset, a key procurement dimension supporting vendor spend analysis."
    },
    {
      "name": "department_assignment",
      "supports_focus": true,
      "rationale": "Attributes the asset/expense to a consuming department, enabling cost allocation analysis around the focus."
    },
    {
      "name": "processing_delay_indicator",
      "supports_focus": true,
      "rationale": "A process-efficiency facet of the expense record; somewhat peripheral to the asset-procurement focus but still an actionable operational attribute of the same records."
    },
    {
      "name": "asset_intended_use",
      "supports_focus": true,
      "rationale": "Explains why the asset was purchased, deepening the procurement focus and enabling need-vs-spend analysis."
    },
    {
      "name": "record_generation_method",
      "supports_focus": false,
      "rationale": "Data-provenance metadata (auto vs manual entry); relates to record quality rather than the asset-procurement focus, diluting coherence."
    }
  ],
  "focus_coherence": 0.78,
  "structure_quality": 0.8,
  "focus_actionability": 0.85,
  "rationale": "The columns clearly converge on a single inferable focus: IT asset procurement spend within expense records. asset_type_category, vendor_or_manufacturer, department_assignment, and asset_intended_use form a coherent, well-differentiated predictor/attribute set (what, who from, who for, why) at a useful granularity, allowing analyses like vendor concentration, department cost drivers, and need alignment. This is genuinely actionable. Two columns dilute the focus: processing_delay_indicator (operational efficiency facet) and especially record_generation_method (data provenance/quality metadata), which drift toward record-management rather than the procurement focus. The set is not a grab-bag and is not a mere restatement, but the two off-focus columns prevent top scores on coherence."
}

